🚀 Typer — Installation & AI Agent Skills Guide
 
Build beautiful CLI interfaces with Python — fast, intuitive, and auto-generated ✅
 
 
 
📦 Step 1 — Install Typer with  uv 
 
Create a new project
 
bash  
uv init awesome-project --bare
cd awesome-project
uv add typer
 
 
What these commands do:
 
-  uv init awesome-project --bare  → Creates a new folder with only  pyproject.toml 
-  uv add typer  → Installs Typer, updates  pyproject.toml , and creates  uv.lock 
-  uv.lock  → Locks exact versions — reproducible installs on any machine ✅
 
Dependencies included:  typer  comes with  rich  (beautiful output) and  shellingham  (auto-detect shell)
 
 
 
🔧 Step 2 — Activate the Virtual Environment
 
Linux / macOS
 
bash  
source .venv/bin/activate
 
 
Windows PowerShell
 
powershell  
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
 
 
Windows Bash / WSL
 
bash  
source .venv/Scripts/activate
 
 
Enable Shell Completion
 
bash  
typer --install-completion
 
 
⚠️ Restart your terminal for completion to take effect ✅
 
💡 You can also run commands without activating the venv by using:  uv run typer --help 
 
 
 
🤖 Step 3 — Install AI Agent Skills
 
Typer includes official AI coding agent skills bundled right with the package — guidance always matches your exact installed version and updates automatically when you update Typer! 🎯
 
Install Library Skills
 
bash  
uvx library-skills
 
 
💡 What  uvx  does: Alias for  uv tool run  — runs temporarily in isolation while scanning your project dependencies. No permanent installation needed! ✅
 
🧩 Supported AI Agents
 
- ✅ Codex
- ✅ Claude Code → Select  .claude/skills  when prompted
- ✅ Cursor
- ✅ GitHub Copilot
- ✅ Gemini CLI
- ✅ Pi
- ✅ OpenCode
- ✅ Most other coding agents
 
 
 
📝 Quick Recap — Full Workflow
 
bash  
# 1️⃣ Create project
uv init my-cli-app --bare
cd my-cli-app

# 2️⃣ Install Typer
uv add typer

# 3️⃣ Activate venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/macOS
# or .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1  # Windows

# 4️⃣ Enable completion
typer --install-completion

# 5️⃣ Install AI Agent Skills
uvx library-skills
 
 
 
 
💡 Alternative: Using  pip  instead of  uv 
 
bash  
# Create and activate venv first
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # or .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows

# Install Typer
pip install typer
 
 
 
 
